sequenceDiagram
    participant A as Manual / Auto browse
    participant P as Player + clocks
    participant I as Preview input cache
    participant W as Coordinator Worker
    participant M as Media API
    participant D as Two independent Workers
    participant S as Sequential decoder
    participant C as Canvas
    A->>P: load + play
    P->>W: start attempt
    alt Active preview with optional input lease
        P->>I: acquire versioned source, revoke old lease
        alt Complete validated cache hit within budget
            I-->>W: bounded MessagePort reads, memory source
        else Miss or ineligible
            I->>M: one authenticated stream
            M-->>I: bytes
            I-->>W: bounded MessagePort reads, network source
            Note over I,W: Cache reservation deducted from decoder budget, ineligible streams bypass retention
        end
    else No input cache
        W->>M: one authenticated stream
        M-->>W: bytes (retain within input budget)
    end
    alt Independent gate and budget pass
        loop Up to four queued frames / 2 MiB threshold
            W->>W: verify frame and retain latest candidate
            P->>W: media target time
            W->>W: omit expired independent work
            opt Sustained high service load for 8 seconds of effective playback
                P->>W: reduce load once, retain across preview attempts
                W->>W: select on integer 30fps grid, keep source timestamps
            end
            W->>D: decode within four output permits
            D-->>W: indexed RGBA
            W-->>P: ordered frame + media interval
            P->>C: draw when due
            P->>W: return output permit / buffer
        end
        Note over P,D: First paint starts MediaClock, decode lag does not freeze it
        opt Midstream dependency or recoverable child failure
            W->>D: stop children after settling in-flight work
            W->>S: retained input + delivered frame position
            S->>S: replay history to restore canvas (may take seconds)
            Note over W,S: No second HTTP request, replayed frames are not displayed again
            S-->>P: composed frames + decoded horizon, four permits
            Note over P,S: MediaClock retained, available horizon follows decode
        end
    else Gate or budget fails before independent playback
        W->>S: sequential stream, two permits
        S-->>P: composed frames
        Note over P,S: FrameClock can slow playback when the decoded queue runs dry
    end
    A->>P: pause / resume
    P->>P: freeze / resume clock, retain instance
    P->>W: backpressure / resume
    Note over I,W: EOF via same input reader
    W->>W: validate complete RIFF
    W-->>P: validated input
    P->>I: commit only complete matching bytes
    opt Manual playback with remaining loops
        W->>W: wait for outputs, reuse retained input
        Note over W,D: Loop boundary may wait for next decode
    end
    P->>C: final frame + later draw callback
    P-->>A: ended once after media endpoint and valid EOF
    opt Auto browse
        A->>A: advance image / scroll
    end
